WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Good morning, John. I'm headed out on tour next week!

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.920
So expect some travel vlogging.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.240
All the shows are all ages and tickets are out at $20.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.620
And somebody asked me on tumblr...

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.400
"What is the difference between Hank Green and Hank Green and The Perfect Strangers?"

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.300
It's pretty simple.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.660
It's more fun to play music with a band.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.000
And I think it's more fun to listen to music with a band

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.960
And so, some of my friends got together and we made a band

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.280
But we play the same old Hank Green songs

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.060
You'll hear Deathly Hallows and Anglerfish and Strange Charm.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.160
And also some newer songs

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.840
Like I Love Science and Oh J.K Rowling and We are All Bat People.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.560
And even some songs we have never before performed live together.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.180
Like We're All 'Gonna Die, which is a song I recently released.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.380
And also, this song, right here.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.200
Surprise!

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.080
New Song!

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.740
Annie's been Annie for long enough now

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.020
she knows what she will and she won't.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.920
Sometimes she's 'gonna be up when you're down.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.340
She's gonna know things that you don't.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.340
And all of the world isn't here just for you.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.740
Annie being Annie doesn't make you less you.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.280
She's got her own baggage

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.800
She doesn't need yours, too.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.840
And Annie doesn't need your luck.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.640
Annie doesn't need your worry.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.860
And Annie doesn't hate your guts.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.540
But she does need you to get up and get out of her way!

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.900
Do you ever think you're holding her down?

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.100
Do you ever even think to ask why?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.120
If you, my friend

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.220
are stuck on the ground,

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.860
are you terrified that she could fly?

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.560
Oh, maybe it's time you took a look at yourself.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.040
Annie's not a trophy you can keep on your shelf.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.620
She's pulling you through life

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.740
You're putting her through hell.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.020
Oh, Annie doesn't need your luck.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.860
Annie doesn't need your worry.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.200
And Annie doesn't hate your guts.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.660
But she does need you to get up and get out of her way!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.400
I have to ask, as a friend

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.520
a friend to both of you.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.600
So when you hold her close and keep her near.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.140
Is that love or is it fear?

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.600
I have to ask because you have to know.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.640
You only get to keep her if you let her go.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.400
Oh let her go

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.060
Oh let her go

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:58.560
Let her go

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.220
Let her go

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.160
'Cause Annie doesn't need your luck!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.240
And Annie doesn't need your worry!

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.140
And Annie doesn't hate your guts!

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.660
But she just needs you to get up and get out of her way!

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:12.160
Yeah

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.280
Oh get up, and get out of her way!

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:14.780
Boy

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.360
Get up and get out of her way!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.240
Get up and get out of her way!

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.300
Getting ready to go on tour has involved lots of work.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.760
Ah - I have been quite tired.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.620
And recently I got home from work

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.280
And I grabbed some peanut M&amp;Ms

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.140
which are my favourite.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.740
And I went and I laid down on my couch.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.620
So, I wake up a half hour later,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.220
and in my mouth is a half eaten M&amp;M.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.480
It was a weird sensation and flavour

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.240
but I ate it.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.300
And that's the whole story

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.360
I just wanted to tell you that one.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.620
So we have been having some trouble selling as many tickets as we'd like to on tour

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.940
This is kind of strange

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.020
because like with Kansas,

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.200
we're doing amazing!

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.580
But in Los Angeles,

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.200
where there are more people than Kansas,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.380
we're doing not as well.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:57.660
So if you are in Austin, San Diego, Los Angeles, Anaheim or San Francisco.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.700
And you're considering maybe coming to the show...

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.820
consider it... hard.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.660
I'm super excited about it , I hope you will be too.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.980
For me, concerts have always been something that caused me a lot of anxiety.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.000
Like going to shows always freaked me out.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.760
But also those shows are some of my most precious memories.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.280
We strive to be that for the people that come to our shows.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.000
ANd there's one thing that always kind of bugs me about concerts.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.620
it's when I go I kind of 'wanna know as many of the songs as I can.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.060
'Cause it's more fun when I'm, like, singing along and having a good time.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.100
But you never know what they're 'gonna play.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:29.400
So, I have put together a limited - but not complete - set list of some of the songs we're 'gonna be playing.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.600
If you would like to know what those are in advance.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.020
As part of my general strategy

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.200
to get rid of this conception that you have to be the smartest, most knowledgable person

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.720
who knows everything about the band and the act.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.360
No.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.220
Just have a good time!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.800
It's not about looking cool.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.340
And that's it.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:49.000
Coming to you straight form the mouth that once had an M&amp;M in it for a whole half an hour.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.640
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

